 measured in the one coronal MR image.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-1-1_F1"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. (2)</label><caption><p>Typical MR image of a case with right ON. A: 5mm, B: 10mm, C: 15mm and D: 20mm behind eye.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-1-1_F2"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. (3)</label><caption><p>Means &#x000b1; SE of the values from the 4 slices behind the eye are shown. In all parts, the ratio was significantly higher in affected eyes.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-1-1_F3"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1.</label><caption><p>Signal Intensity Ratio (%) in the Case Shown in Fig. (<xref ref-type="fig" rid="F2">2</xref>)</p></caption><table frame="border" rules="all" width="50%"><thead><tr><th rowspan="2" colspan="1"/><th colspan="4" rowspan="1">Distance from Eye</th></tr><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">5mm</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">10mm</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">15mm</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">20mm</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Right Eye</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">154.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">145.3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">104.5</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">121.2</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Left Eye</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">107.6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">85.6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">88.1</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">88.0</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>